<!--- BEGIN NEWS ENTRIES --->
	<!--- 3/19/04 --->
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="760" colspan="2" class="bigyellow">March 19th, 2004 - Johnny Ying Yang and other noteworthy moments<br><img src="images/line.gif" width="760" height="2" border="0" alt=""></td>
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="150"><img src="images/mobs/solro.jpg" width="200" height="150" border="0" alt=""></td>
				<td>I think Seinfeld said it best one day at the bakery. "I love the black and white. 
				If people would only look to the cookie. All our problems would be solved." <br><br>
				How does this relate to us you ask?  Well, as Jerry learned later on, sometimes you get the cookie,
				sometimes the cookie gets you (7 years down the drain).  Last time the black and white got us, this
				time we strapped on our shitkickers and brought a big glass of milk, he didn't stand a chance.<br>
				Gratz on your Plane of Fire access, well deserved.<br><br>
				In other news the House Archon real life gathering took place this past weekend at which members
				from all walks of life gathered to see who the biggest geek was.  Gratz Arch for finding the computer
				within 30 minutes of your arrival.  While I can't reveal too much information due to the top sekrit nature
				of all HA gatherings (which is odd seeing this was our first) I can tell you a few things:<br>  1. Canadians do
				indeed have flappy heads and use words like aboot and eh all the fucking time. <br> 2. Dwarf clerics from Denmark
				can drink anyone *ANYONE* under the table and then drink the table.<br> 3. Rafghar is really a redneck (and he 
				really did manaburn himself). <br> 4. NYC in March is cold, like a dogs balls freezing to the porch cold (poor Deud 
				found that out the hard way.) <br> <br>
				All other info has been tossed in the vault, if you wish to learn such things you will just have to apply.
				<br> <br>
				-Vent <br>
			</td>
			</tr>
	<!--- 2/20/04 --->
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="760" colspan="2" class="bigyellow">February 20th, 2004 - Rallos Zek falls to the Archons<br><img src="images/line.gif" width="760" height="2" border="0" alt=""></td>
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="150"><img src="images/mobs/rallos.jpg" width="150" height="200" border="0" alt=""></td>
				<td>And that ain't half bad.  It seems that night the monkey had lost its football, normally this is a cause for much monkey frustration.  
				I mean without the football who gets the luvin?  Well it turns out that despite being an axe wielding maniac Rallos Zek was unable to resist
				the ape phermomones, either that or he looked like a football which forced us to sexxor him up against his will.  It really was a plan of genius.
				  You see we lulled him into a false sense of security by pretending to be inept for a few days, then once we were sure that he was complacent 
				  that we could not defeat him, we put forth our best effort and nailed him before he had any chance to run away.  This is actually quite 
				  similiar to Ilainya's dating mentality although Rallos is much lighter (and prettier) then Ilainya's normal saturday night conquest. 
				  It should also be noted that Rafghar did die and I am pretty sure Strykin cried, but that was because he wasn't on and now has to be 
				  backflagged.<br><br>
					What does all this mean you ask?  Well it is pretty simple, House Archon now has access to the elemental planes and Malys has 3 whole new zones
				in which he may leave bodies.  Both are things of beauty.  Gratz and well deserved Archons.<br>
				<img src="images/nakid.jpg" width="600" height="255" border="0" alt=""><br>
				<img src="images/kami.jpg"><br>
				<img src="images/zori.jpg"><br>
				<img src="images/kung.jpg"><br>
			</td>
			</tr>
		<!---1/9/04--->
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="760" colspan="2" class="bigyellow">January 9th, 2004 - Paladin Gimpness<br><img src="images/line.gif" width="760" height="2" border="0" alt=""></td>
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="150"><img src="images/mobs/mithmarr.jpg" width="150" height="150" border="0" alt=""></td>
				<td>Remember how I promised you some pictures of lewts?  Well I lied. Sorta.<br> <br>
			I mean I thought about cutting and pasting and cropping and fitting about 140 drops and then I realized
			something very important.  I am not on crack.  You see this is important because the only way I could make
			it through such a posting session would to be completely blitzed out of my skull.  <br><br>
			Content with that idea I bring you good tidings!  Mithaniel Marr has been killed.  And we are no contently on
			our way to the Tower of Solusek Ro.   Many were concerned, could we do it with such numbers on our first attempt?
			We cowered in a huddle mass in the corner until we came to a realization:  He is a pally and therefore gimp.
			But he is the god of all paladins! you say.  That is true, but being the god of all gimps just makes him a bigger gimp.
			Anyway after much consoling to Surewright and Banewrath (who suicided themselves on the nearest orc pawn after the kill) 
			we have the first of our flags and now get to start the whole process over for those who may have missed it.  HUZZAH!
			</td>
			</tr>
		<!--- 1/08/04 --->
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="760" colspan="2" class="bigyellow">January 8th, 2004 - All outta bubblegum<br><img src="images/line.gif" width="760" height="2" border="0" alt=""></td>
			<tr valign="top">
				<td width="150"><img src="images/mobs/tallon.jpg" width="150" height="150" border="0" alt=""></td>
				<td>Well shit, a lot has happened in the last month.  First, as I am sure you are aware by now we have ourselves a new look. I call it Quake meets Everquest.
				It has the homestlye feeling you have come to expect from HA and yet a taste of a frag count lingers in the air.  Brilliant!  Lets all give thanks to Crumbeness
				having more ambtion then I could and taking it upon himself to redesign the site. <br><br>
				Now onto the stuff you outsiders care about.  What has the House been up to?  Well it seems that the fire under our asses has been lit and the Planes
				of Power has taken the full on force of that anger.  Where to start,  where to start.  In no particular order we have 3 full Vex Thal clearings, 2 Emp bashing, a Lord Inquisitor Seru smashing
				a couple of Agnarr's (they wouldn't let me kill Karana, whiny ass rangers!) 2 Bertox pummelings, a Tallon & Vallon Zek double whammy, the 3 Halls of Honor trials (twice~)
				and a Saryn in a pear tree!  What does all this mean?  Hell if I know, although the cries for backflagging can be heard across the land. <br><br>Now I know your asking, "Jesus were did you find the time for all this?"
				Well seeing Jesus doesn't play Everquest, son of God only plays FPS games and MarioKart, I shall answer in his place.  It took a lot of Mountain Dew, some take out Chinese, 3 large boxes of kittens and most of my sanity.  
				I think the officers had something to do with it as well, damn their ambition! <br> <br>
				But Ventur where is all the loot you ask?  My response:  Piss off! you know how much loot was involved?  Actually seeing I am still filled with the holiday spirit I may post some over the next day or two, so stay tuned, same bat time same bat channel!<br><br></td>
			</tr>
	
	<!--- END NEWS --->
				
				</td>
			</tr>
